Computation modules for muti-energy systems sizing: This tool is a software tool designed to support the techno-economic and environmental optimisation of multi-energy systems. The software reads case-study data from structured CSV input files, models energy demands and assets such as generators, converters, storage systems, fuels, electricity/energy network imports and exports, electric vehicle fleets, shiftable loads, and controllable thermal loads, and builds a mathematical optimisation model using Pyomo. The model is solved with the HiGHS solver and can optimise different objectives, including net present value minimisation, CO₂ emissions minimisation, and renewable energy integration maximisation, while also considering optional user-defined constraints related to investment, maintenance, emissions, CO₂ costs, and renewable integration. The software exports detailed operational and sizing results to CSV files, including asset capacities, system costs, energy imports and exports, fuel use, EV charging and discharging profiles, load-shifting results, and thermal comfort-related profiles. The result consists of the implemented computational workflow, input-processing routines, optimisation model formulation, demand-response modules, electric vehicle and storage modelling, asset-sizing logic, and automated result-export procedures.

This software is authored by:
António Manuel Freitas Coelho
Bruna Daniela Costa Tavares
